  "2026-10-15T21:46:03.696Z",codex-agent,"Catalog Swarm validation on implementation dc63489 reproduces the existing deadline/cancellation class. Initial pm-linked HTTP run under overlap: 3 total, 1 pass, 1 fail, 1 canceled, 0 skips; built server canceled at 300000.145243ms and source server then reports stateError spawn ENOTDIR at test/catalog-install-e2e.test.ts:115. Independent direct built-server scenario passes at 268798.261578ms. This change adds Swarm catalog data and installation-refusal assertions; it changes no command runtime or deadlines. Preserve the failed run; standalone release and non-overlapping linked HTTP verification are pending."
  "2026-10-15T22:33:31.216Z",codex-agent,"Contrasting final catalog Swarm acceptance on unchanged implementation dc63489: full isolated npm and Bun release gates both pass 601/601 with zero failures/cancellations/skips. npm HTTP built/source cases pass at 254189.02205ms/188243.174177ms; Bun at 166200.268747ms/189986.526424ms, all below unchanged 300000ms deadlines. Capacity and packed consumers pass 1/1 and 4/4 in each gate. Keep the earlier pm-linked timeout/cancellation cascade as failed evidence; this catalog metadata change does not repair scheduling sensitivity. Item remains unclosed."
  "2026-10-15T23:51:42.904Z",codex-agent,"Catalog metadata refresh pm-web-5hdb initial isolated npm gate: 605 total, 597 pass, 7 fail, 1 cancelled, 0 skips. Built Presets acceptance exhausted 300000 ms at 303134 ms; following source case reported spawn ENOTDIR. Other unchanged startup deadlines failed: graph activation exceeded 30000 ms and returned HTTP 424 after installation; both fatal-JSON children reached their 10000 ms timeout/SIGTERM; both observable-realtime cases failed server startup readiness before their functional/privacy assertions. Catalog command runtime and these test/runtime files are unchanged from main. New catalog drift and canonical command-freshness checks passed. Retain failed evidence; one unchanged isolated npm retry is planned."
  "2026-10-16T00:42:10.930Z",codex-agent,"Final all-entry catalog candidate: isolated npm suite completes 606 total, 603 pass, 2 fail, 1 cancelled, zero skips. Built Presets passes at 283688.730 ms, while source Presets reaches the unchanged 300000 ms deadline at 300001.563 ms. The unchanged missing-DATABASE_URL entrypoint test reaches its 10000 ms child deadline at 10166.165 ms without a child exit code. Other initial-attempt startup/provisioning/fatal-log cases pass in this run. No timing assertion, command runtime or threshold changed. Independent Bun gate follows."
  "2026-10-16T01:08:49.011Z",codex-agent,"Independent final-code Bun release gate exits at coverage: 606 total, 604 pass, 1 fail, 1 cancelled, zero skipped. Built Presets reaches the unchanged 300000 ms deadline at 300007.375 ms; the following source scenario fails with spawn ENOTDIR at 6139.878 ms, matching the retained cancellation cascade. Other startup/fatal-log/readiness checks pass. Catalog command runtime and these acceptance tests are unchanged from main. Full npm remains failed 603/606; neither aggregate gate is accepted. No assertions or thresholds were changed."
  "2026-10-16T04:32:35.537Z",codex-agent,"Route/bootstrap coverage candidate reproduces the existing cancellation cascade under isolated CI identity: built Presets cancelled at 300007 ms, then source install returns HTTP 400 with spawn ENOTDIR at the install assertion. Both cases passed in the initial baseline (the only baseline failures were partial-fleet catalog discovery). No package command implementation or deadline changed. Full instrumented counters: 634 total, 631 pass, 2 fail, 1 cancelled, zero skips; separate graph latency failure is recorded on pm-web-hqqp. All 16 new route/bootstrap tests pass. Preserve this failed evidence; repeated full release gates follow."
  "2026-10-16T06:43:55.893Z",codex-agent,"Contrasting final route/bootstrap acceptance on unchanged package-command implementation and unchanged 300-second deadlines: four final-floor npm/Bun release gates pass completely (two per runtime), each 634/634 with zero fail/cancel/skip/todo, capacity 1/1 and packed consumers 4/4. Built/source catalog times: npm final 1 224.478/245.383 seconds; Bun final 1 145.065/134.188; npm final 2 147.491/117.690; Bun final 2 117.180/133.498. Preserve earlier timeout and spawn ENOTDIR failures as separate failed evidence; this coverage change does not repair scheduling sensitivity. Item remains unclosed."
  "2026-10-16T10:02:09.704Z",codex-agent,"PR #209 review round 1 isolated npm run release:check exits 1 at coverage: 637 tests, 636 pass, 1 fail, zero cancelled/skipped/todo. The unchanged test/smoke.test.ts production server bootstrap listens on an ephemeral port and answers HTTP child exits code=1 signal=null before listening at 1069.956 ms, with empty stderr. That rejection omits its captured stdout, so neither a timing cause nor an initialization/bind cause is established. All three new cleanup regressions and all route/bootstrap cases pass. Failed-run instrumentation reports statements/lines 92.42, branches 80.69, functions 95.90, above unchanged floors, but no accepted coverage receipt or full release pass is claimed; downstream phases were not reached. Reusing this existing startup investigation rather than filing a duplicate. Independent focused startup and Bun evidence follow."
  "2026-10-16T10:14:07.219Z",codex-agent,"Contrasting review-round evidence with unchanged startup code and assertions: the isolated focused command node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern='production server bootstrap listens' test/smoke.test.ts passes 1/1 at 1234.686 ms. The independent isolated bun run release:check coverage phase passes 637/637, including the same smoke case at 2136.886 ms, zero fail/cancel/skip/todo and all 37 source files above unchanged floors. Its capacity phase also passes 1/1 and production audit reports zero vulnerabilities; remaining packed/release phases are pending. The npm aggregate remains failed 636/637; no root cause or startup repair is claimed. Keep the failure and this follow-up open."
  "2026-10-16T13:53:53.525Z",codex-agent,"Reader-lock mitigation pm-web-bazs reproduces the existing catalog cancellation signature on unchanged catalog code/deadlines. npm run release:check is fully green: 646/646, 2/2 capacity, 4/4 packed; configured-source coverage 92.47 statements/lines, 81.00 branches, 96.02 functions. Sequential bun run release:check ends at coverage: 646 total, 644 pass, 1 fail, 1 cancelled, 0 skipped/todo. Built catalog acceptance timed out at 300000.797 ms; source case then reported stateError spawn ENOTDIR at its initial catalog assertion (5128.997 ms). Incomplete run coverage 91.61 statements/lines, 80.65 branches, 95.69 functions, failing the unchanged 92.07 statements/lines floors. Same isolated Git identity and disposable Postgres setup; shared-host load elevated. The catalog test constructs createApp directly and starts no mutation watcher. Reuse this existing follow-up rather than creating a duplicate; no catalog code or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-17T04:16:06.679Z",codex-agent,"PR #216 round 2 reproduced the existing full-release failures without changing server runtime or server tests: npm and Bun each ran 666 tests with 663 passed, 2 failed, 1 canceled, 0 skipped and 0 todo. In both attempts the built catalog consumer hit 300000 ms, then the source variant reported spawn ENOTDIR. The npm attempt also reproduced pm-web-fhob's first/end-first then independent ordering; the Bun attempt reproduced pm-web-hqqp's 2000-item read limit at 10691 ms versus 10000 ms. Statement/line coverage was 91.76% and 92.01%, below the unchanged 92.07% floor. These are failed local attempts, not release acceptance. No thresholds or deadlines were relaxed. Exact-head CI remains required for the UI-only round."
  "2026-10-17T11:01:40.292Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 acceptance again reproduces the built catalog-consumer 300-second deadline and source process startup failure under isolated Git identity. Both the package worktree npm attempt and the independent standalone Bun attempt hit the consumer/startup cases; standalone catalog membership/snapshot checks pass. All 258 TypeScript/CSS source files match between profiles. Server code, deadlines and coverage floors are unchanged; final full-run counts are recorded with pm-web-i0td."
  "2026-10-18T03:22:25.625Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 isolated npm and Bun release attempts reproduce the existing built catalog consumer 300-second timeout, followed by source-variant startup failure. Both use unchanged suite deadlines and isolated Git identity. Full counts will follow after the runners finish. This review changes no catalog/runtime consumer code or budgets; clean-runner CI remains a separate required result."
  "2026-10-18T03:42:26.185Z",codex-agent,"Completed isolated round 4 npm and Bun release attempts each execute 667 tests: 663 pass, 3 fail, 1 canceled, 0 skipped, 0 todo. The 300-second built catalog timeout is canceled; the source consumer returns spawn ENOTDIR. The other failures are canonical pm-rust command-snapshot drift (new follow-up pm-web-5e1q) and the tracked 2000-item graph wall-time budget (pm-web-hqqp). Both changed clear-field and SSE regressions pass within both full attempts. npm statement/line coverage is 91.94%, branches 81.06%, functions 95.80%; Bun measures 92.07%, 81.34%, 95.80%. These attempts are failures and not exact-head acceptance; their prechecks began before the final browser-only initial-fit helper refactor. Clean-runner final-head CI is required separately."
